    <bioghist encodinganalog="545$a">
      <head>Historical Information
</head>
       <p>When Virginia Governor James Gilmore left office in 2002, he sent an incomplete set of his gubernatorial records to the the Library of Virginia, prompting State Librarian Nolan Yelich to demand that the public records be transferred as required by law. After months of mediation an agreement was reached between the two parties and the balance of the records were transferred to the Library of Virginia in November 2002.
</p>
      





    </bioghist>




    <scopecontent encodinganalog="520$a">
      <head>Scope and Content
</head>
      <p>Records related to the transfer of the Governor James S. Gilmore papers to the Library of Virginia, 2002-2004, document the dispute between the Library of Virginia and Virginia Governor James S. Gilmore (1998-2002) over the disposition of his gubernatorial records.  This collection contains the records of State Librarian Nolan Yelich, State Archiviest Conley Edwards and State Records Administrator Preston Huff.  Records may include correspondence, agreements, court records, drafts, meeting notes, memorandums, newspaper clippings, and press releases related to records management and archival issues. State Records Administrator records also include two folders related to Governor Allen and Governor Warner.
</p>





    </scopecontent>
